From 9e2ec00f6911d101f49b8023cb8596dec719c59f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Boyd Milan <jersonboyd@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 10:56:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Document exp_pauli, givens_rotation and fermionic_swap

These three operations were reachable from user code but absent from the
documentation (#2141).

* Add an `exp_pauli` section to the Quantum Operations page, stating the
  `exp(i theta P)` convention, the Pauli-word ordering rule, and both the
  register and variadic call forms in Python and C++.
* List `givens_rotation` and `fermionic_swap` among the documented
  `PyKernel` methods, and expand their docstrings with the definition and
  unitary matrix of each rotation, so that the API reference explains what
  the operations do rather than only that they exist.
* Correct the sign in the `applyExpPauli` doc comment: the base
  implementation decomposes into `rz(-2 * theta)`, which applies
  `exp(i theta P)`, matching the Quake `exp_pauli` op and the C++ and
  Python builder documentation.

Matrices and the sign convention were verified numerically against the
existing decompositions.

Signed-off-by: Boyd Milan <jersonboyd@icloud.com>
